<hr class="border-border-l2 clear-both">
<h3 dir="auto" class="font-semibold text-xl max-md:font-display max-md:text-heading-3 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:tracking-[0px] max-md:mb-3 max-md:mt-3">Why not an Unsplash link?</h3>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">I cannot upload the generated image to Unsplash.</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A random Unsplash URL is not “your” Cybertruck Foundation image.</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">A local <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">/products/...</span> path is the correct, fastest option for your Next.js app.</li>
</ul>
<hr class="border-border-l2 clear-both">
<h3 dir="auto" class="font-semibold text-xl max-md:font-display max-md:text-heading-3 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:tracking-[0px] max-md:mb-3 max-md:mt-3">If you want the <strong class="font-semibold">new</strong> generated image instead</h3>
<ol dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
