e: none; border-top-width: medium; border-right-color: ; border-right-style: ; border-right-width: ; border-bottom-color: ; border-bottom-style: ; border-bottom-width: ; border-left-color: ; border-left-style: ; border-left-width: ; border-image-source: ; border-image-slice: ; border-image-width: ; border-image-outset: ; border-image-repeat: ; padding: 0px 16px 16px; margin-top: 0px; font-size: 0.9em; font-family: var(--font-ibm-plex-mono); line-height: 1.5em; background-color: hsl(var(--surface-inset)); color: var(--fg-primary); display: block; overflow: auto;"><pre class="shiki slack-dark" tabindex="0" style="background-color: rgb(34, 34, 34); color: rgb(230, 230, 230);"><code><span class="line"><span>https://www.image2url.com/r2/default/images/1786368701445-dba54f5e-b108-45de-bd69-7ce4c38f91bd.blob</span></span></code></pre></div><div></div></div><div class="false flex flex-col gap-2 h-full"></div></div></div>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">Open that URL in a <strong class="font-semibold">new browser tab</strong>.</p>
<ul dir="auto" class="marker:text-secondary">
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">If you <strong class="font-semibold">don’t</strong> see the Cybertruck image → the link is bad; re-upload and copy a direct image link (usually ends in <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">.jpg</span> / <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">.png</span> / <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">.webp</span>).</li>
<li class="break-words whitespace-pre-wrap [&amp;&gt;ul]:whitespace-normal [&amp;&gt;ol]:whitespace-normal">If you <strong class="font-semibold">do</strong> see the image → after clearing localStorage it should appear on the site.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0" style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><strong class="font-semibold">4. Confirm in code</strong></p>
<p dir="auto" class="break-words last:mb-0 max-md:leading-[155%] max-md:mb-4 max-md:last:mb-0" style="white-space: pre-wrap;">In <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">store.ts</span> for <span class="text-sm px-1 rounded-sm !font-mono bg-orange-400/10 text-orange-500 dark:bg-orange-300/10 dark:text-orange-300">inv-1</span> you should have:</p>
